  "configuration_id": "config_045",
  "reason": "1) Evidence: The strongest signal across all 9 completed experiments is the RNA encoder choice — pca_n2000 outperforms scgpt by ~0.06 in rna_only and ~0.10 in multimodal settings. The current best (config_009: pca_n2000 + ViT + avgpool + weighted, acc 0.635) is built on PCA, but scvi_n200 has not been tested at all, leaving a critical gap in our understanding of which RNA representation is optimal. 2) Question: config_045 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) isolates the effect of the RNA encoder by holding every other design choice at its best-known value (ViT image encoder, avgpool aggregation, weighted fusion, multiprofile). This gives a clean single-variable comparison against config_009. 3) Why this is the best use of the next experiment: The RNA representation is the highest-impact design axis (the pca-vs-scgpt gap was the largest single effect observed), and we have zero data on scvi_n200. If scvi_n200 matches or beats PCA, it opens a new promising direction; if it falls well short, it confirms PCA's dominance and lets us focus remaining budget on fusion/aggregation refinements. Either outcome substantially reduces uncertainty on the most important design decision, making this the highest-information experiment available."
}

